{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.78ef07af49","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_poss","group":"poss-5","passage":"<p>All three ______ manuscripts arrived at the publisher on Monday.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["authors's","authors","author's","authors'"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Decide between plural and possessive forms: the manuscripts belong to several authors, so the plural possessive “authors'” is correct."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.802e0e662a","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_poss","group":"poss-6","passage":"<p>All three ______ times were recorded by the officials.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["runners's","runners'","runner's","runners"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Decide between plural and possessive forms: the times belong to several runners, so the plural possessive “runners'” is correct."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.d49296b263","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-2","passage":"<p>The school board announced that ______ new schedule had been approved.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["it's","their","its","they're"],"answer":"C","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the school board,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.f5d92dada1","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-3","passage":"<p>The city council announced that ______ decision surprised many observers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["their","its","they're","it's"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the city council,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.54d2a6a190","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-7","passage":"<p>The university announced that ______ plan for the summer included several community events.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["they're","their","it's","its"],"answer":"D","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the university,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.13fa307548","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-10","passage":"<p>The club announced that ______ latest report was available online.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["its","it's","they're","their"],"answer":"A","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the club,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.3977c1bbb6","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-11","passage":"<p>The committee announced that ______ annual budget would be released next week.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["their","its","they're","it's"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the committee,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.d86c85b1b9","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_tense","group":"tense-0","passage":"<p>Over the past decade, the city ______ three new public libraries.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["had opened","has opened","will open","opened"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “Over the past decade,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has opened.”"}
